hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24047","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from a man of Banu Harithah, that a man stabbed a she-camel in its throat with a peg, fearing it would escape him. So he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded him, or commanded them, to eat it."
